helm (4.3.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Build from upstream's source at the 4.3.2 tag, rather than repacking the
    release binary. The series version suffix is added at build time by
    .forgejo/registry-upload and never committed.
  * The repack had reached zero advisories only for as long as the trivy
    database stood still. 4.3.1 as released now scans with five -- two in
    x/net (CVE-2026-78661, CVE-2026-97045) and two in the standard library
    of Go 1.27.2 (CVE-2026-111943, CVE-2026-97054), plus GO-2026-5932 --
    and 4.3.2 as released still scans with one, because upstream built it
    with Go 1.27.3 and x/crypto 0.58.0. A release binary cannot be
    remediated; only a rebuild can.
  * So the build now pins what upstream could not: Go 1.27.4 through
    GOTOOLCHAIN, x/crypto 0.59.0 (which removed the openpgp package
    GO-2026-5932 is about) and x/net 0.63.0. The result scans with no
    findings at any severity.
  * debian/upstream-sha256 is replaced by debian/upstream-commit, since
    there is no longer a tarball to checksum: the build clones the release
    tag and refuses to continue unless HEAD is the recorded commit.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:35:00 -0500
